{"availability":"available","full":"linjunway/SMS-Classifier","name":"SMS-Classifier","description":"Deploying a production ready SMS Classifier via industry tools. Accuracy of the model has been tested and pushed to its absolute limit given the constraints of a limited dataset and library toolkit.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T11:00:40Z","updated":"2026-10-09T12:25:09Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sms-classifier-1.streamlit.app/","topics":["data-preprocessing-and-cleaning","docker","fastapi","feature-engineering","scikitlearn-machine-learning","streamlit"],"demo":"https://sms-classifier-1.streamlit.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T16:52:44.829Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T16:52:44.829Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T16:52:44.829Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T08:00:41.559Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T16:52:44.829Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["End-to-end ML engineering project: from research notebook to a tested, containerised, continuously deployed service.","SMS phishing (\"smishing\") is hard to catch because it looks a lot like ordinary promotional spam. This project classifies a message as Normal, Spam or Smishing with a two-stage scikit-learn ensemble trained on fewer than 3,000 messages (96.6 % accuracy, 89.1 % balanced accuracy on 2,986 held-out messages), and wraps it in the tooling a real service needs:","🔗 Live demo: · API docs (when running): /docs"],"features":["Serving: a validated, documented REST API (FastAPI) plus an interactive Streamlit demo.","Reproducibility: one shared preprocessing path for training and serving, pinned dependencies, fixed seeds, Docker images that train the model during the build.","Automation: every push to main is linted, tested and Docker-built by GitHub Actions, and the live demo redeploys automatically (see CI/CD & deployment)."],"sourceU